{
  "summary": "This experiment tested an RNA-only multiprofile model using scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder, achieving 65.0% validation accuracy (vs. 59.1% for the PCA_n2000 baseline) and 62.8% F1. The result suggests the RNA encoder choice may influence performance, though uncertainty remains about whether other factors (e.g., interactions with aggregation or profile settings) contribute to the improvement. No direct comparisons to alternative encoders or fusion strategies were conducted."
}

